like, 15 people were in.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:53.580
It was like 4:00 in the morning,
and that's when I first saw her.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.115 line:92%
And it was -- She turned it out.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's always like, "I wish
you don't remember that show."

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.320
She killed. It was, like,
this after-hours place.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I saw her
at the Laugh Factory,

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I was aware of her
as a comic.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, in a way,
you're sort of putting togethe

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
a superhero team
when you cast these movies

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it strikes me
that you have this, like,

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.133 line:92%
sort of multigenerational cast

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:16.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it must be tastes of yours
from when you're a kid.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, for example,
when you have James Earl Jones

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:21.674
And then, obviously, younger
actors who you've obviously seen

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thought, "They're
going to be great in this.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.712 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Absolutely. Absolutely.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:28.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did a movie years ago,
"Harlem Nights,"

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.683 line:92%
with Richard Pryor and Red Foxx.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was another one
of those movies

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
where it was older generatio
and the new comics.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
Robin Harris --
a great comic that passed away

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:40.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was in the movie, as well
And my brother Charlie.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yeah,
I kind of get a kick out of,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.064 size:75% position:38%
